triage judged: investigate (low confidence, suspects unknown)
  A single warning on a datastore's rate metric is not clearly a benign latency blip, and a database-level anomaly can precede broader failure, so it is not safe to dismiss. No open incident matches and nothing in the signal points to a specific fault class yet.
investigation: 2 round(s), 5 dispatch(es), 18 step(s)

=== PROPOSAL ===
  ABSTAINED - no permitted action fits the evidence
  if wrong    : If a Loki query past 15:02:30 shows mongodb-rate still absent or looping startup/SIGTERM, and a kubelet/pod-event check shows no external killer still active, then restart_service becomes justified and this abstention was too cautious. Conversely, if pod events name the fault-injection ConfigMap as the killer, a restart would be re-killed and the fix lies outside this system.
  rests on    : tr_9948fd3a2026, tr_fcd9d6881852, tr_596c016954c3
  execution   : not executed - a proposal is a claim, never the change (ADR-0028 §1)

context: 20884 pushed / 5168 pulled (pull rate 0.1984), 2 section(s) dropped

=== VERDICT ===
  fault class : process_freeze
  fix class   : restart
  confidence  : low
  evidence    : tr_9948fd3a2026, tr_fcd9d6881852, tr_616998c15f26, tr_4d3c551d555b, tr_596c016954c3
  root cause  : mongodb-rate's pod was created fresh at ~15:01 by platform-automation and then terminated externally by SIGTERM (kill(2) from pid 0/uid 0) within seconds, twice: two clean WiredTiger startup cycles at 15:01:02 and 15:01:04 each ended in signal-handler-driven orderly shutdown, the last at 15:01:10 [tr_9948fd3a2026][tr_fcd9d6881852]. The service itself logged no errors and its storage engine opened, recovered and checkpointed cleanly, so neither corruption, disk, nor storage misconfiguration is the mechanism [tr_fcd9d6881852][tr_4d3c551d555b]. The change set is a first-time workload creation accompanied by a ConfigMap whose name indicates fault-injection/failure-administration intent, landing seconds before the container came up [tr_616998c15f26]. The best-supported reading is an injected/administered kill of the mongodb-rate process: the datastore is absent from the topology while its socket/endpoint churns, leaving callers in the hotel-reservation namespace without a rate datastore. With no metrics available for this service at all [tr_596c016954c3], the mechanism is the process being stopped/killed rather than any value being wrong.
  OPEN        : Whether the SIGTERM came from the fault-injection ConfigMap, normal Kubernetes pod lifecycle/rescheduling during first creation, or a liveness-probe failure - no kubelet or pod-event evidence was gathered.
  OPEN        : Whether mongodb-rate stayed down after 15:01:10 or recovered; the log window ends at 15:02:30 and no post-onset startup was observed.
  OPEN        : Which callers (e.g. rate service) actually degraded, and whether they hung to deadline or failed fast - no upstream metrics or logs were dispatched.
  OPEN        : What alert fired at 15:02:21 and on what signal, given Prometheus holds no series for this service [tr_596c016954c3].

